1 NAME Levin /Goldschmidt/
2 GIVN Levin
2 _MARNM Goldschmidt
1 SEX M
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} There were five Jewish households in Salzuflen in 1719, one of them was that of Levin Goldschmidt, a son of the Hoffaktor Samuel Goldschmidt. Before 1717 Levin had returned from Amsterdam to Lippe-Detmold. When he 
2 CONC submitted his request to settle in Salzuflen he declared that he intended to trade in "Dutch goods" (source: Historische Handbuch der jüdischen Gemeinschaften in Westfalen und Lippe: Die Ortschaften und Territorien im heutigen Reg
2 CONC ierungsbezirk Detmold, p. 201).
2 CONT
2 CONT He may be identical with "Levin Goldsmit", who is mentioned in Amsterdam in 1708 in the notarial records.
