1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shimon_Sofer  '''Rabbi Shimon Sofer'''] (1820–1883) (German: Simon Schreiber) was a prominent Orthodox Jewish Rabbi in the 19th century. He was Chief Rabbi of Kraków, Poland after serv
2 CONC ing as Chief Rabbi of Mattersdorf. He was the second son of the famous Rabbi Moshe Sofer (Chassam Sofer) of Pressburg.
2 CONT
2 CONT As president of the Orthodox Jewish party Machzikei HaDas, Sofer was a member of the Polenklub at the Reichsrat under the Austria-Hungary monarch Franz Joseph I. He was elected as Deputy of the Kolomyia district of Galicia. As a H
2 CONC alakhist and Talmudist he authored commentary and responsa in a work known today as Michtav Sofer.
2 CONT
2 CONT 	יארצייט:יז אדר ראשון, ה'תרמג
2 CONT
