2 CONT Avraham Jakob Stern (born in 1768), learned watchmaking in Hrubieszow. His skill and energy came to the attention of the priest S. Staszyc, who - although known as an enemy of Israel - gave Stern his patronage and supported his st
2 CONC udies. Later on, Stern invented a calculating machine, together with his brother-in-law, Chaim Zelig Szlonimski, the first editor of the Hebrew periodical “Hatsefira” . They were given a prize of a thousand rubles by the Tsar. Ste
2 CONC rn translated into Polish the book of Natan Nute Hannover, “ Yon Metsula”, on the disturbances of 1648.
