3 CITY Berlin
3 STAE Berlin
3 CTRY Germany
1 DEAT
2 DATE 13 MAY 1859
2 ADDR
3 CITY Vienna
3 STAE Vienna
3 CTRY Austria
1 TITL Freifrau
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Henriette von Pereira-Arnstein (29 November 1780 – 13 May 1859) was an Austrian pianist and salon-holder.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henriette von Pereira-Arnstein was born in Berlin in 1780, daughter of the Viennese banker Nathan von Arnstein and his wife Fanny von Arnstein, who maintained an upper-class salon in Vienna frequented by artists, musicians, diplom
2 CONC ats and politicians.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henriette was educated at her parents' home, and she studied the piano with 
2 CONT
2 CONT Muzio Clementi and Johann Andreas Streicher. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married in 1802 the banker Heinrich Freiherr von Pereira (1773–1835);
2 CONT
2 CONT  they had three sons and a daughter.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of her mother in 1818, she continued her mother's salons, but on a smaller scale and less formally. They took place on Fridays and there were musical performances, including herself as pianist. Her guests included 
2 CONC musicians Ludwig van Beethoven, Felix Mendelssohn and Franz Liszt; and poets Franz Grillparzer, Theodor Körner and Clemens Brentano. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She had a strong friendship with Theodor Körner, and his song cycle Leier und Schwert ("Lyre and Sword") was written for her.
2 CONT
2 CONT Like her mother, she was involved in many charities; she was director of the Marienspital in Baden bei Wien. She died in Vienna in 1859.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT "Die Grabschriften des Alten Judenfriedhofes in Wien" 
2 CONT
2 CONT Band II- by Dr. Bernhard Wachstein-pg. 464
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography in german: https://www.biographien.ac.at/oebl/oebl_P/Pereira-Arnstein_Henriette_1780_1859.xml
2 CONT
