2 CONT The Jewish Chronicle - July 16 1926
2 CONT
2 CONT Dr. WALTER CASTLE.
2 CONT
2 CONT The death, at the early age of thirty-four, of Dr. Walter Castle, removes one who was confidently expected to win a foremost place in the medical world. A specialist in Dermatology, he had won a high reputation, and held staff app
2 CONC ointments at several hospitals. The deceased, who was educated at Wellington College, distinguished himself highly in all forms of sport. At the outbreak of war he joined the navy as a surgeon, and served both in the North Sea and
2 CONC  in the Baltic, being awarded the Distinguished. Service Cross for conspicuous gallantry. At Cambridge, he took the Natural Science Tripos, and became M.B., M.D., and M.R.C.S. (London). The deceased was greatly beloved by his pati
2 CONC ents, whom he treated always with the utmost kindliness and care. He married in 1921, Kathleen, daughter of Mr. and Mrs. Charles P. Seligman, by whom he had a son and a daughter.
