2 CONT As a national economist, Moritz Julius Bonn (1873–1965), who was of Jewish extraction, was among the leading economics experts of Weimar Germany. Bonn participated in the peace negotiations in Versailles as an expert on reparation
2 CONC s, and he served as the expert on reparations in the German Chancellery from 1920 to 1922.
