1 CONT In February 1900 Orlik had great success with his first one-man exhibition in Brünn in Austria,
1 CONT showing works in many media. It was at this time that Max Lehr introduced Orlik to Marie von 
1 CONT Gomperz and her family. Her father, Max von Gomperz was a wealthy industrialist and patron of 
1 CONT the arts. He bought from and commissioned many paintings and other works by Orlik. Marie
1 CONT Gomperz and Orlik developed a life-long friendship documented through their correspondence
1 CONT which continued until the time of Orlik's death. The extensive Gomperz collection of his work
1 CONT was exhibited at the Jewish Museum in Vienna in 1997. Orlik's oeuvre reflects this patronage 
1 CONT and friendship through many portraits of members of the family and of their country estate of
1 CONT Oslawan in Slovakia and its surroundings.
0 @N6000000002802158280@ NOTE
