0 @N6000000006374355254@ NOTE Id#: 0096310
1 CONT Name: Feiss, Julius
1 CONT Date: Jul 8 1931
1 CONT Source: Cemetery record;  Cleveland Necrology File, Reel #024.
1 CONT Notes: Feiss: Julius, suddenly, Monday, July 6, at his residence, 1672 Oakwood Dr. Services at Mayfield Chapel, Wednesday, 2:30 p. m. Please omit flowers. 1848 - 1931. Mayfield Cemetery Cleveland, Ohio.
0 @N6000000000475290807@ NOTE Thomas Plonsker reported that he saw , on his great grandfather's grave (Max Plonsker ,in Cologne)
1 CONT an inscription:
1 CONT In memory of Mrs. Lina Plonsker (Max's wife = Otto's Mother)
1 CONT Miss. Jenny Schloss (Lina's Sister)
1 CONT Herbert & Erna Plonsker
1 CONT Killed in KZ
1 CONT We have no other information to substantiate this and his wife's name.
0 @N6000000000475293014@ NOTE Otto converted to Catholicism in 1925, and the rumors have it, that this was Martha's condition, for their marriage.
1 CONT In accordance with letters from Curt Plonsker, who had written contact with his wife, He was employed in a Post Office, in Bremen.
1 CONT
1 CONT He was taken to Terzin Camp, with his mother Carolina (nee Schloss) but survived and returned to his home in 1946. After about 6 Month he left his family without notice, then remarried Walburga.
0 @N6000000000475290786@ NOTE In accordance with informatio contained in letters from Curt Plonsker:
1 CONT Curt met him once in Hamburg, where he worked in a bank, as a clerk.
1 CONT
1 CONT Thomas Plonsker found in the archive of Trier that in 1939, he was forced to add  "Israel" to his name.
1 CONT
1 CONT During the Nazi days he escaped and hid in Holland, for about 7 years, with the help of his wife.
1 CONT
1 CONT When hearing from Curt, he requested Curt to help in obtaining immigration papers into the US, but Curt,
1 CONT who received the papers for his immigration from a Plonsker, in Chicago, who was actually not related-
1 CONT was unable to help due to being a newcomer to the US himself. Thus he could not provide the required 5 years support guarantee to Heinrich and his wife.
1 CONT Heinrich became annoyed and so the contact broke up.
1 CONT
1 CONT He visited in Israel, with Kaethe, his 1st wife, abt. 1958 and met with the family of Hans Plonsker, in Tel Aviv.
0 @N6000000004212631083@ NOTE
1 CONT Deposited money in Swiss Bank, but forgot the account number!
1 CONT 15 Jun 5708
